{"name":"Magnolia","hex":"#fff9e4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Magnolia","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Magnoliaceae – magnolias."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name from English, one of the less common flower names invented in the 19th century.","Several places in the United States.\nA city, the county seat of Columbia County, Arkansas, United States.\nA town in Delaware, United States.\nA village in Illinois, United States.\nA city in Iowa, United States.\nA coastal village in the city of Gloucester, Essex County, Massachusetts. \nA town in Minnesota, United States.\nA city, the county seat of Pike County, Mississippi, United States.\nA borough in Camden County, New Jersey. \nA town in North Carolina, United States.\nA village in Ohio, United States.\nA city in Texas, United States.\nAn unincorporated community in West Virginia, United States.\nA town in Wisconsin, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Magnolia"}],"entries":[{"title":"Magnolia","blocks":[{"text":"Magnolia is a large genus of about 210 to 340 flowering plant species in the subfamily Magnolioideae of the family Magnoliaceae. The natural range of Magnolia species is disjunct, with a main center in east, south and southeast Asia and a secondary center in South America, Central America, the West Indies, and some species in eastern North America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Magnolia_sieboldii_flower_1.jpg/330px-Magnolia_sieboldii_flower_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magnolia","wikidata":"Q157017"},{"title":"Magnolia (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Magnolia is a 1999 American drama film written, directed and co-produced by Paul Thomas Anderson. It stars an ensemble cast, including Jeremy Blackman, Tom Cruise, Melinda Dillon, Philip Baker Hall, Philip Seymour Hoffman, Ricky Jay, William H. Macy, Alfred Molina, Julianne Moore, John C. Reilly, Jason Robards, and Melora Walters. The film is an epic mosaic of interrelated characters in search of happiness, forgiveness, and meaning in the San Fernando Valley. The script was inspired by the music of Aimee Mann, who contributed several songs to its soundtrack."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4b/Magnolia_poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magnolia_(film)","wikidata":"Q588420"},{"title":"Magnolia (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Magnolia is a color named after the flowering plant of the genus Magnolia. As magnolias have flowers of more than one color, mainly cream or pale purple, magnolia may refer to different colors in different countries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Magnolia_wieseneri.jpg/330px-Magnolia_wieseneri.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magnolia_(color)","wikidata":"Q6731851"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Magnoliafruitopen.JPG/500px-Magnoliafruitopen.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Magnoliafruitopen.JPG/1280px-Magnoliafruitopen.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Magnoliafruitopen.JPG/500px-Magnoliafruitopen.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMagnoliafruitopen.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Magnolia_biondii.jpg/500px-Magnolia_biondii.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/c